{"assign":{"step":7,"landed_at":"2026-09-25T15:38:08-05:00","outcome":"**The CSS audit landed: up to 8,599 of 35,769 lines can go, and a pick-a-curve page for container-unit padding.** Eight module audits, an explorer, the ranked plan and the padding curves are done. The ai2.css pilot was not run.\n\n- [CSS explorer](/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/): every directory in a twirl-down tree with rolled-up line counts; click one for its verdicts and proposal.\n- [Ranked reduction plan](/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/plan/): biggest savings first, each with its risk. The top five are deleting `core/new` (up to 1,851 lines), the moved `imagine/` twins (1,749), repointing three importers (949), `Panel/toolbar.css` (142) and one shared chip (321).\n- [Padding curves](/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/tokens/): today's `--pad` against three container-unit curves at 1280, 1920 and 3440. The builder recommends A, `clamp(1rem, 2.5cqi, 4rem)`. Pick one; `framework.css` is untouched.\n\nThe savings are ceilings: I spot-checked five verdicts and three were right. A wrong delete (`.all-pad` still used in a demo) and a wrong duplicate (`.ai-ask` is not `.card`) show the DUPLICATE and DELETE claims need a side-by-side check before anything is removed.\n\nLeft open:\n- The ai2.css pilot was skipped: spend reached about $17 against the $15 budget, and no curve is approved yet. It also needs the explorer's AI 2 verdicts confirmed first.\n- The layout-check task's landing is inferred from commit `b052c869`; I could not message it.\n- The explorer builder mentioned a console-noise caveat that came through truncated; I did not chase it.","links":[{"url":"/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/","label":"CSS explorer"},{"url":"/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/plan/","label":"Ranked reduction plan"},{"url":"/framework/ai/2026-09-25/css-audit/tokens/","label":"Padding curves"}],"tokens":null}}
